Simulations can be run using the "namd3 [filename].conf", where [filename] should be replaced with the appropriate name.

The input files for performing the simulations shown in the associated manuscript are located in the deca-alanine
folder. The Deca-Alanine folder within contains the ABF simulations with C-C and C-C groups distances as the CVs.
The Deca-Alanine_WTM-eABF folder within contains the WTM-eABF simulations with C-C, C-C groups, RMSD and HBonds as CVs.

The simulations are present in the respective calculations folders, while the common folder contains the force-field.

In all cases the abf.conf files is the input and the Distance.in file contains the colvars configuration.
